      "problem": "$\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) & =\\frac{{e}^{2\\sqrt{3}}-1}{{e}^{2\\sqrt{3}}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
